  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0206, and it contains three tables: Region, Flora_and_Fauna_Record, and Environmental_Change_Record. The Region table has four columns: Administrator, Geographical_Location, Name, and Region_ID, with Region_ID being the primary key. The Flora_and_Fauna_Record table has seven columns: Quantity, Record_ID, Record_Time, Recorder, Region_ID, Type, and FOREIGN KEY (Region_ID) REFERENCES Region(Region_ID). The Environmental_Change_Record table has eight columns: Change_ID, Change_Time, Humidity, Location, Rainfall, Region_ID, Temperature, and FOREIGN KEY (Region_ID) REFERENCES Region(Region_ID). The Region_ID column in both tables is a foreign key that references the Region table's Region_ID column.",
  "gold_question": "Business requirements for the ecological protection zone management system: An ecological protection zone needs to manage multiple areas, each of which has an area number, name, geographic location, and administrator. The protection zone needs to record the species and number of plants and animals in each area. Each record needs to include the plant and animal record number, record time, recorder, plant and animal species, and number. The system also needs to record environmental changes within the protection zone, including environmental change record number, temperature, humidity, rainfall, etc., and indicate the time and location of the change.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0206.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0206\nCREATE TABLE `Region` (\n  `Region_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Administrator` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Geographical_Location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Region_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Flora_and_Fauna_Record` (\n  `Record_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Record_Time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Recorder` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Region_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Record_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `flora_and_fauna_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Region_ID`) REFERENCES `Region` (`Region_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Environmental_Change_Record` (\n  `Change_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Change_Time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Humidity` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Rainfall` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Region_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Temperature` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Change_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `environmental_change_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Region_ID`) REFERENCES `Region` (`Region_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
